    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the other files are base/helper classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the immutable structured audit event for owner creation, in addition to the existing audit line.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `OwnerCreatedEvent.java` (`rest/function/owner/`):\n- An immutable `record OwnerCreatedEvent(long seq, Integer ownerId, String customerCode, Integer membershipLevel, String event)`, serialized by Jackson to exactly `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n- A factory `of(long seq, Owner owner)` that is **the single site resolving the owner's primary identifier** \u2014 today `owner.getCustomerCode()`. Per the spec's forward requirement, when the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, only this one method changes so the event then carries the memberId instead.\n\n**Changed** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Kept the human-readable audit line unchanged.\n- Added a static `AtomicLong SEQ` giving a monotonically increasing sequence across creates.\n- Injected the Spring-provided `tools.jackson.databind.ObjectMapper` as a function parameter (by-type injection, still one public method per the OfficeFloor rules) and emitted `AUDIT.info(mapper.writeValueAsString(event))`.\n\nObserved output confirms both records:\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...\nINFO  AUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nThe acceptance test `coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` \u2014 which asserts one AUDIT message contains `OWNER_CREATED`, the owner id, and the customerCode value \u2014 passes, and the project compiles cleanly.",
